{
 "summary": "The collected evidence does not show a checkout outage. Gateway, inventory and orders all report a 0% 5xx ratio and normal p95 latency (136ms, 45ms and 98ms) for the whole window. No root cause can be identified: there is no evidence from any checkout or payment service, no traces, logs or deploy records, and nothing from in front of the gateway.",
 "root_cause": null,
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway request rate ended the window at 1.56 req/s, below its 1.95 req/s average and 2.24 req/s peak. That could mean some traffic is not reaching the gateway, but it is a modest drop and could be normal variation.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory and orders request rates also ended below their averages (1.10 vs ~1.33 req/s), in step with the gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5859ba914c39",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "A server-side 5xx failure or latency cascade at the gateway is not supported: 5xx ratio was 0.0% max and p95 latency peaked at 182ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory errors or slowness are not supported: 0.0% 5xx and p95 at most 47ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5859ba914c39"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders errors or slowness are not supported: 0.0% 5xx and p95 at most 100ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "No metrics for a checkout, payment, cart or frontend service were collected. The failing path may be in a service outside this evidence.",
  "The metrics only count 5xx. 4xx responses, client-side errors, or failures returned with HTTP 200 (business-logic errors) would not show up.",
  "No traces, logs or deployment records are in the snapshot, so recent changes and per-request failures cannot be checked.",
  "Nothing in front of the gateway (CDN, load balancer, DNS, TLS, frontend app) is covered. Failures there would never reach the gateway and would show only as lower traffic.",
  "The pre-incident baseline request rate is unknown, so it is unclear whether ~1.5–2 req/s at the gateway is normal or a large drop in traffic.",
  "No customer-facing report or synthetic check is included to confirm the outage or show which step of checkout fails."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Reproduce a checkout end to end (synthetic or manual) and note the exact failing step and the response returned.",
   "rationale": "The backend services in evidence look healthy, so the failure point must be found directly.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Collect metrics, traces and logs for the checkout and payment services and any third-party payment provider, and widen the query to include 4xx rates.",
   "rationale": "The only services queried show no errors. The fault is likely in an uncovered service or appears as a non-5xx failure.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-5859ba914c39",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check the edge layer (CDN, load balancer, DNS, TLS certificates, frontend deploys) and compare gateway traffic with its normal baseline.",
   "rationale": "Gateway traffic fell toward the end of the window. That fits requests failing before they reach the gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Pull deployment and config-change records for all services and the frontend around 09:40–09:54 UTC.",
   "rationale": "No deploy data was collected, so a recent change cannot be ruled in or out.",
   "evidence_ids": []
  }
 ]
}
